  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Morodok Baitang</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  .The Morodok Baitang activity fosters sustainable, conservation-friendly, climate-smart, and socially equitable economic growth for Cambodians. The activity supports strategic partnerships between rural communities, private sector actors, and their development partners to increase revenues and employment opportunities; and to accelerate economic diversification to improve livelihoods, attract investment, and create jobs. ..Morodok Baitang builds on prior and current USAID investments in biodiversity conservation, low emissions development, improved livelihoods for natural resource-dependent communities, and natural resource governance, but has a stronger focus on improving conditions for private sector investment and sustainability of USAID&apos;s efforts. USAID awarded the activity to Tetra Tech ARD and three sub-contractors including Wildlife Conservation Society, Dalberg, and Mekong Strategic Partners, through a competitive process in which the offeror with the best value to the U.S. government was selected, in accordance with federal procurement regulations. .The activity falls under the administration&apos;s &quot;Promoting net-zero, climate-resilient future&quot; priority by working with relevant stakeholders to promote technology that enhance community resilience and contribute to low emission development. The activity contributes to achieving USAID/Cambodia&apos;s CDCS 2020-2025 Development Objective 1, &quot;Inclusive and sustainable economic growth broadened&quot; and the ICS Mission Objective 2.1, Sub-objective 2.1.2, &quot;By 2024, civil society and private sector actors have improved management of and sustainable and accountable development practices on two million hectares of biodiverse and biologically significant areas&quot; through interventions that conserve Cambodia&apos;s unique biodiversity and improve accountable and equitable economic development.... .</narrative>
  </description>
